 2. 🏛️ Speaker bows out 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 House Speaker Mike Johnson campaigns for Rep. Derrick Van Orden in Platteville, Wis., last week. Photo: John Moore/Getty Images Speaker Mike Johnson (R-La.) plans to step down as the House's top Republican after the GOP's epic midterm election losses wiped out his party's majority, Axios' Kate Santaliz reports. 

 📝 Johnson told colleagues in a letter that his decision wasn't easy, but that the demands of serving in leadership had required significant sacrifices from his family.

 He wrote: "After three years in this role, I believe the time has come for me to give them more of the attention and presence they so richly deserve." ( Read his letter .) Johnson's exit touches off a potentially contentious scramble to replace him.

 House Majority Leader Steve Scalise (R-La.) and Judiciary Committee Chair Jim Jordan (R-Ohio) have both thrown their hats in the ring. 🗳️ What's next: House Republicans are set to hold leadership elections on Nov. 10.

