 4. 📸 Pic to go: Making history 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Reba Saldanha/AP Rep. Chris Pappas (D-N.H.), at right above, is set to become the first openly gay male U.S. senator , after beating Republican John Sununu in New Hampshire.

 Pappas is shown with his husband, Vann Bentley , last night at a victory party in Manchester, N.H. Pappas' campaign focused on issues like affordability, health care and political corruption. 🎤 The senator-elect said in a victory speech last night: "Whether you're a Republican, an independent or a Democrat, tonight's victory is for you, because this is a victory for team New Hampshire over the broken status quo that is hurting all of us just the same."

